# Line endings, settled once here rather than per machine.
#
# This repository is worked on from a Mac and from a Windows PC. Without this
# file, Git on Windows checks every text file out with CRLF and commits it back
# with CRLF, so a pull on the Mac can show hundreds of files as modified with no
# real change in any of them -- and a genuine one-line fix becomes impossible to
# review. Forcing LF in the working tree on both machines avoids the churn
# entirely; every editor in use here handles LF on Windows without complaint.
#
# No tracked file contained CRLF when this was added, so it renormalises nothing
# and the first Windows checkout after it lands is the only one that changes.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and Git hooks must be LF whatever happens -- /bin/sh fails with
# a confusing "not found" if a shebang line ends in CR.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/** text eol=lf

# Lockfiles are generated: collapse them by default in GitHub's review view,
# which is where their size is actually in the way. Deliberately NOT marked
# -diff -- that would make `git diff` report them as binary, and a lockfile is
# exactly where a dependency swapped for a malicious version would hide.
package-lock.json linguist-generated

# Binary: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.docx binary
*.pem binary
